title ALES178 — Lotus's stereo_vibrato: the wet-only triangle-LFO modulated delay carried into stereo, the SAME LFO on BOTH channels, each channel read off ITS OWN frozen snapshot — the third rung of the stereo MODULATION class and the FIRST that snapshots
prompt Autonomous loop lap after ALES177: take the next agent-doable crux Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think ALES176/177 opened the stereo modulation class with the two THIN per-sample modulations (tremolo, ring modulator) — every output depends only on its own input sample, so both write in place with NO snapshot. The class's other half is the delay-line modulations, none yet carried into stereo. Crux-first: the vibrato (ALES72) is the thinnest of chorus/vibrato/flanger — the delayed voice heard ALONE, wet-only, no dry mixed under it and no mix level, so four faults and no BadLevel. The honest first delay-line stereo lift, the crux the SNAPSHOT discipline rather than the arithmetic (ALES72's reused verbatim). The prior ALES177 log predicted exactly this next rung.
think vibrato's four checks were inline, so factored them into a shared pub precheck(clip_len, start, count, centre, depth, period) mirroring ALES75's ring_mod.precheck, and had mono vibrato call it; ales_vibrato_witness re-ran GREEN (additive). Then composed stereo_vibrato mirroring stereo_ring_mod: StereoVibratoError = vibrato.VibratoError reused whole, validate ONCE against the shared length before either channel is snapshotted, then run vibrato.vibrato per channel with the SAME LFO. The honest new thing vs the thin pair: each channel reads its OWN frozen snapshot (mono vibrato snapshots its own clip's dry prefix), so no cross-channel snapshot — the mono discipline twice, nothing threaded across the seam.
think Proved four laws: stereo vibrato law (each channel == mono vibrato byte for byte, channels genuinely differing); chorus-family law (a full-wet stereo chorus == the dry master plus this stereo vibrato PER CHANNEL sample for sample, proven against ALES71's mono chorus run per channel — the family identity chorus[i] = saturate(dry[i] + vibrato[i]) carried to two channels); image law (identical-channel master stays identical AND a right-is-half-left pan keeps its L:R ratio sample for sample, the interpolation a convex combination linear in the input and the wet voice off the rail); balance/silence/atomicity/degenerate (four refusals — BadPeriod, BadDepth, BadDelay, BadRange — each leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count 0 the identity).
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; witness GREEN through Rishi, TAME style bans clean (opening triad, ≥2 asserts/fn with // invariant, no @memcpy, named errors with try, triangle+interpolation in i64, saturate a proven no-op on the convex-combination wet voice), scan roster clean. The stereo modulation class now holds the amplitude pair (tremolo, ring modulator) AND its first delay-line rung (vibrato); the next Lindy rungs carry the chorus (dry+wet mix, a BadLevel returns) and the flanger (a feedback path reading the live per-channel buffer — the harder crux), or auto_pan.
